{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help manage stomach acid reflux, focus on foods that are low in acid, high in fiber, or have soothing properties.\n\nGood food choices include:\n*   **Fruits:** Bananas, melons (like watermelon, cantaloupe, and honeydew), and apples are often recommended due to their low acidity or alkaline nature.\n*   **Vegetables:** Most green vegetables such as asparagus, broccoli, Brussels sprouts, kale, spinach, leafy greens, cucumbers, and green beans are excellent as they are low in fat and alkaline. Potatoes, carrots, sweet potatoes, and beets are also good options.\n*   **Grains:** High-fiber whole grains like oatmeal, brown rice, whole grain breads, and cous-cous can help absorb stomach acid.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Skinless chicken and turkey, fish (especially oily fish like salmon), seafood, tofu, and egg whites are good low-fat protein sources.\n*   **Other:** Ginger (especially in tea), skim or fat-free yogurt, unsweetened coconut water, and nuts (like walnuts and almonds) can also be beneficial. Foods with high water content such as celery and broths can help dilute stomach acid.\n\nRemember to avoid deep-frying meats and be mindful of how vegetables are prepared, as high-fat additions like butter can worsen symptoms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:3": 4.9103738079022365, "clueweb22-en0009-09-00824:2": 4.825457459352139, "clueweb22-en0039-65-00093:3": 4.807695909596237, "clueweb22-en0005-41-09262:15": 4.798857379087235, "clueweb22-en0044-72-05971:1": 4.709332968564811, "clueweb22-en0021-74-19197:1": 4.657335118119957, "clueweb22-en0039-15-05920:17": 4.654708889777541, "clueweb22-en0024-83-01996:17": 4.638761773005576, "clueweb22-en0039-15-05920:18": 4.594460269277063, "clueweb22-en0018-80-17587:11": 4.542327567653144, "clueweb22-en0034-72-18979:1": 4.518796239463798, "clueweb22-en0034-72-18979:0": 4.5126281