{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help manage acid reflux, several lifestyle and dietary strategies can be beneficial.\nFirstly, adjust your eating habits: opt for smaller, more frequent meals throughout the day instead of large ones, and avoid eating within 2-3 hours of bedtime to allow for proper digestion before lying down. Eating slowly and chewing your food thoroughly can also help. Keeping a food and symptom diary can help you identify and avoid your personal triggers, as these can vary.\nSecondly, focus on lifestyle modifications. Maintaining a healthy weight is crucial, as excess weight can put pressure on your stomach. Quitting smoking and limiting alcohol intake are highly recommended, as they can relax the esophageal sphincter.\nConsider elevating the head of your bed by 4-6 inches or using a wedge pillow to prevent acid from rising during sleep. Wearing loose-fitting clothing and avoiding tight belts can also ease pressure on your stomach. Managing stress through techniques like meditation or exercise can contribute to overall well-being and potentially reduce symptoms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0034-91-08129:2": 4.813858610336362, "clueweb22-en0005-19-04103:5": 4.387883724079727, "clueweb22-en0003-24-03853:5": 4.2535211468315355, "clueweb22-en0016-83-09082:8": 4.198651293943792, "clueweb22-en0038-68-03750:10": 4.108411359660724, "clueweb22-en0032-79-13642:8": 4.08108810675585, "clueweb22-en0036-14-03464:13": 4.021501722180183, "clueweb22-en0028-64-19668:3": 3.9666136432093615, "clueweb22-en0033-11-03857:10": 3.9114521014022667}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0034-91-08129:2": 4.813858610336362, "clueweb22-en0037-74-14945:10": 4.676328434815521, "clueweb22-en0005-19-04103:5": 4.387883724079727, "clueweb22-en0027-58-19039:6": 4.371439267696888, "clueweb22-en0003-24-03853:5": 4.2535211468315355, "clueweb22-en0025-45