{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To continue your journey towards a healthier and more active lifestyle, here are some practical next steps focusing on key areas:\n\n**Exercise:** Aim for at least 150 minutes of moderate physical activity weekly, including brisk walking, jogging, or dancing, and incorporate strength training 2-3 times a week. Look for opportunities to be more active in your daily tasks, like taking the stairs or moving every 30-60 minutes. Starting small and gradually increasing activity can make it more sustainable.\n\n**Diet:** Focus on eating mostly minimally-processed whole foods, including plenty of fruits, vegetables, and lean proteins. Make an effort to get enough protein with each meal to support your goal. While you eat out regularly and late, try to balance your diet by choosing healthier options and planning meals to cook at home more often.\n\n**Sleep:** Prioritize getting 7-9 hours of quality sleep nightly. Establish a regular sleep schedule, going to bed and waking up at the same time each day. Reduce caffeine intake, especially in the afternoon, and avoid napping in the evening.\n\n**Screen Time:** Set boundaries with your phone usage, especially given your desire to stop doom scrolling. Power down your devices and avoid screen time for at least an hour or two before bed to improve sleep hygiene.\n\n**Stress Management:** Practice positive coping techniques like deep breathing, spending time in nature, or engaging in hobbies you enjoy, such as 3D printing. Regular exercise and adequate sleep are also excellent stress relievers. Remember to set boundaries and take time for yourself.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-86-05045:6": 3.572301753891978, "clueweb22-en0020-09-06440:3": 3.562717772253394, "clueweb22-en0002-85-13122:16": 3.250315025378623, "clueweb22-en0041-32-12053:10": 3.1416961502509015, "clueweb22-en0028-73-1524