{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage your weight, focus on practical, sustainable lifestyle changes. Start by assessing your current habits and identifying areas for improvement, such as snacking or portion sizes (12).\n\nFor diet, prioritize nutritious meals rich in fruits, vegetables, lean protein, and whole grains (4, 8, 10, 13). Reduce processed foods, sweets, unhealthy fats, and excess calories (4, 13, 14). Practice portion control, paying attention to hunger and fullness cues, and avoid \"supersizing\" meals (9, 10). Plan meals and snacks, eat mindfully, and track your food intake using a diary or app to identify patterns (7, 15, 16, 17). Learning to cook can also help you make healthier choices (14).\n\nIncorporate regular physical activity into your routine. Aim for at least 30 minutes of exercise most days, including activities like walking, jogging, swimming, or biking (7, 8, 11, 13). Add motion to your day by taking stairs or parking further away (7, 13). Strength training a few times a week can also be beneficial (18).\n\nBeyond diet and exercise, prioritize sleep, aiming for 7-9 hours per night, as insufficient sleep is linked to higher body weight (5, 15). Manage stress, as it can contribute to overeating (6, 12). Weigh yourself regularly to catch weight changes early (5, 14, 20). Remember, gradual, consistent changes are key for long-term success (12, 20). If you have specific health concerns or obesity, consult your doctor for personalized advice (4, 11).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0028-48-02988:13": 4.1782528366817155, "clueweb22-en0031-07-12408:16": 4.15812399448523, "clueweb22-en0036-58-05974:12": 4.155083261587607, "clueweb22-en0022-54-00983:1": 4.151276794102099, "clueweb22-en0010-18-15537:5": 4.112136112686104, "clueweb22-en0044-06-01696:14": 4.099125896503759, "clueweb22-en0036-27-10877:9": 4.036806630172571, "clueweb22-en