{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Yes, garlic can indeed help boost your metabolism! Several studies and properties of garlic contribute to this effect.\n\nOne way garlic works is by stimulating the release of norepinephrine, a neurotransmitter that increases your body's metabolism, helping you burn calories faster (Passages 3, 5). It can also slightly raise your body's temperature, which encourages fat breakdown and speeds up metabolism (Passage 1).\n\nFurthermore, garlic has been shown to normalize blood sugar levels, improve blood flow, and help your body process \"good\" cholesterol while fighting \"bad\" cholesterol, all of which contribute to a healthier metabolism (Passage 2). Research also suggests that garlic may help by \"turning off\" genes involved in storing fat, which can lead to reductions in body weight and fat (Passage 20).\n\nBeyond boosting metabolism, garlic is also known to suppress appetite, helping you feel fuller for longer and reducing overeating (Passages 3, 4, 13).\n\nTo incorporate garlic into your diet, you can simply add fresh cloves to your regular cooking (Passage 16). Some recommendations suggest having one clove of garlic daily, either mashed and mixed with water and lime juice, or included in your recipes (Passages 7, 10).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0005-37-20318:3": 4.962944032927783, "clueweb22-en0020-36-05174:16": 4.845526854651828, "clueweb22-en0004-67-10066:1": 4.584244703524957, "clueweb22-en0022-33-16740:14": 4.578046258877394, "clueweb22-en0004-06-07544:2": 4.512029788187904, "clueweb22-en0032-66-14669:6": 4.385344031429368, "clueweb22-en0032-66-14669:5": 4.226901450758779, "clueweb22-en0014-80-17264:2": 4.0720386855646105, "clueweb22-en0020-36-05174:17": 4.019122078457401, "clueweb22-en0041-89-08008:4": 3.891770834636677}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0005-37-20318:3": 4.9629440329277