{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Choosing the right running shoes is crucial for comfort, performance, and injury prevention. The best advice is to visit a specialty running store. They can provide professional help, often using gait analysis or 3D foot scans, to help you understand your foot type (e.g., arch, pronation) and how you move.\n\nWhen trying on shoes, prioritize comfort above all else. The shoe should feel like an extension of your body, not something you're constantly aware of. Ensure there's about a thumb's width of space between your longest toe and the end of the shoe, as your feet expand during a run. Don't assume your size or stick to a brand based on marketing; try on various styles and brands.\n\nConsider the terrain you'll be running on (e.g., road for your 10km in New York) and look for shoes with appropriate cushioning and support. Finally, remember not to wear brand new shoes on race day; they should be broken in, ideally having been used for at least 100 miles.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0016-81-12613:9": 4.715193519548824, "clueweb22-en0042-93-05771:15": 4.580875600484901, "clueweb22-en0033-26-12679:2": 4.567994887983531, "clueweb22-en0031-37-17290:4": 4.538261428697115, "clueweb22-en0033-26-12679:1": 4.359786332625487, "clueweb22-en0017-51-11925:4": 4.344917876543705, "clueweb22-en0004-94-13132:12": 4.286580187974187, "clueweb22-en0043-98-06837:3": 4.234374623586753, "clueweb22-en0000-57-00537:11": 4.230319592771317, "clueweb22-en0045-66-09625:7": 4.212435605108247, "clueweb22-en0025-17-01935:3": 4.199616729782857, "clueweb22-en0032-57-03681:10": 4.186691430524929, "clueweb22-en0026-47-01829:11": 4.179658812595853}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0000-41-18655:0": 4.813889484657299, "clueweb22-en0019-45-05584:2": 4.770398765446865, "clueweb22-en0016-81-12613:9": 4.715193519548824, "clueweb22-en0042-93-0