{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Given your interest in Spanish culture, history, and rare books, I have a few excellent suggestions for you in New York City.\n\nA top recommendation is the **Hispanic Society Museum & Library** in Upper Manhattan. It is dedicated to the art and culture of Spain and its former colonies. Its library boasts an impressive collection of over 250,000 books, including 15,000 rare books printed before 1700, such as a first edition of *Don Quijote*. You can also see the \"Sorolla Room\" featuring 14 massive paintings depicting scenes from regions of Spain.\n\nYou might also be interested in exploring the historical area known as **\"Little Spain\"** on West 14th Street in Manhattan. This neighborhood served as a social and cultural hub for Spanish immigrants from the late 19th century. While smaller today, places like the **Spanish Benevolent Society** (La Nacional) were central to the community, and the documentary \"Little Spain\" traces its history.\n\nFor a broader Latin American cultural experience, consider **El Museo del Barrio** in Upper Manhattan, devoted to Latin American culture, or **Mil Mundos Books and Cafe** in Bushwick, offering English and Spanish books.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:8": 4.852694322228835, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:4": 4.820855785666565, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:9": 4.774301452273143, "clueweb22-en0033-89-11446:4": 4.681767603633802, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:0": 4.637545452712018, "clueweb22-en0035-03-12701:2": 4.432322562746091, "clueweb22-en0011-89-10290:5": 4.238876023572619, "clueweb22-en0012-83-04827:1": 3.915422725846757, "clueweb22-en0033-89-11446:3": 3.8787788141114374, "clueweb22-en0035-03-12701:0": 3.44633458602686, "clueweb22-en0024-98-05137:2": 3.412146358210095, "clueweb22-en0012-68-09657:4": 3.3536986369409556, "clueweb22-en0012-68-09657:5": 3.3450332186251854}, "