{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "New York City offers a wide variety of excellent spots for training, catering to different fitness preferences and levels.\n\nFor comprehensive gym facilities, major chains like **Equinox**, **Crunch**, **New York Sports Clubs**, and **David Barton Gyms** are popular choices, offering a range of classes including yoga, Pilates, spinning, and strength training, often with amenities like saunas and juice bars. The **Sports Center at Chelsea Piers** is a massive complex featuring areas for running, rock climbing, basketball, volleyball, boxing, and swimming. Other notable gyms include **Ludlow Fitness**, **Mid City Gym**, and the **New York Athletic Club**.\n\nIf you're interested in specific types of workouts, you can find high-intensity interval training (HIIT) and boxing classes at places like **Rumble Boxing** or **Sweat440**, which provides full-body workouts. For rock climbing, popular indoor gyms include **Brooklyn Boulders**, **Cliffs at LIC**, and **Steep Rock Bouldering**. There are also specialized studios for cycling (e.g., **Soulcycle**, **Flywheel**) and dance-based workouts.\n\nFor outdoor training, **Central Park** is a fantastic option, where you can find organized bootcamps like **Outdoor Training C.A.M.P. XT** or simply go for a run. You can also find personal trainers through services like FitnessTrainer.com or Leading Edge NY who can customize sessions and meet you at convenient locations, including parks or even your accommodation.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0008-95-04168:1": 3.554496014182429, "clueweb22-en0017-56-04685:5": 3.3419797879836888, "clueweb22-en0043-97-05545:15": 3.165450441212869, "clueweb22-en0040-76-16515:3": 3.1627307024066367, "clueweb22-en0021-36-15243:0": 3.119804364749344, "clueweb22-en0007-27-12737:5": 3.0561937338468432, "clueweb22-en0013-52-08158:9": 3.0550560649430856, "clue