{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For a healthy breakfast focusing on high protein, low carb, and calcium, there are several excellent ingredient choices.\n\nFor **protein**, eggs are a versatile and top choice. You can make veggie frittatas, scrambled eggs, or even a mozzarella and egg breakfast sandwich. Greek yogurt is another fantastic option, offering high protein and calcium, especially when plain to avoid added sugars. Protein shakes are also a fulfilling and customizable way to get your protein, and can easily be made low-carb. Nuts and seeds like almonds, walnuts, chia seeds, hemp seeds, and flaxseed meal are great additions for protein and healthy fats. Cottage cheese and low-fat cheeses also provide good protein and calcium. Lean meats like turkey ham or salmon can also be incorporated.\n\nTo keep it **low-carb**, focus on ingredients like eggs, avocado, and Greek yogurt, which are good alternatives to refined carbs. Smoothies can be made low-carb by using bases like almond or coconut milk, keto yogurt, protein powder, and ingredients such as berries, cucumber, and avocado. Specific low-carb breakfast ideas include Power Greens Breakfast Casserole or a Guacamole and Egg Breakfast Bowl.\n\nFor **calcium**, Greek yogurt, milk, and various low-fat dairy products like cottage cheese, ricotta cheese, and other low-fat cheeses are excellent sources.\n\nBy combining these elements, you can create a balanced and nutritious breakfast that meets your goals.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0040-10-14443:7": 4.964011781336529, "clueweb22-en0022-86-04257:1": 4.6083931742160695, "clueweb22-en0023-35-02978:7": 4.549194929247169, "clueweb22-en0015-75-08687:7": 4.461961767576293, "clueweb22-en0043-96-12285:2": 4.402063831574878, "clueweb22-en0040-10-14443:6": 4.3263966904976865, "clueweb22-en0038-32-15171:3": 4.31972989996108, "clueweb22-en0028-96-01184:4": 4.234