{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "During pregnancy and while breastfeeding, your body's demand for calcium significantly increases to support both your health and your baby's development. Calcium is crucial for building strong bones and teeth, and it helps your circulatory, muscular, and nervous systems function properly. If you don't get enough calcium, your baby will draw what it needs from your bones.\n\nIt's recommended that pregnant and breastfeeding women aim for 1,000 mg of calcium each day. Good dietary sources of calcium include:\n*   Low-fat dairy products like milk, yogurt, and cheese.\n*   Calcium-fortified options such as orange juice, milk-alternatives, and cereals.\n*   Dark green, leafy vegetables like kale, broccoli, collard greens, and bok choy.\n*   Canned sardines and salmon with bones.\n*   Tofu.\n*   Nuts and seeds, including almonds, and corn tortillas.\n\nIf you're concerned about your calcium intake, your healthcare provider may also recommend supplements, but it's always best to get nutrients from a varied diet first.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-79-07034:1": 4.594483858365498, "clueweb22-en0045-34-06591:6": 4.242217972441275, "clueweb22-en0034-27-16750:2": 4.096448793830245, "clueweb22-en0038-56-16380:8": 3.952180721596479, "clueweb22-en0013-05-13235:13": 3.870403839867874, "clueweb22-en0045-34-06591:1": 3.85258959807454}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0035-79-07034:1": 4.594483858365498, "clueweb22-en0000-09-19416:1": 4.529010309105374, "clueweb22-en0025-72-11996:0": 4.427092516326797, "clueweb22-en0037-95-16785:0": 4.395244770495925, "clueweb22-en0007-10-16832:0": 4.31651573417121, "clueweb22-en0045-34-06591:6": 4.242217972441275, "clueweb22-en0009-25-07321:2": 4.184435620493721, "clueweb22-en0034-27-16750:2": 4.096448793830245, "clueweb22-en0030-34-07541:5": 4.08989891152031, "clueweb22-en0035-79-