{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "CO2 laser treatment works by emitting short, concentrated beams of light produced by electricity running through a gas-filled tube. This light targets water molecules in your skin, vaporizing surface skin cells of the epidermis. This process removes the outer layers of aged or sun-damaged skin, making way for fresh, clear new skin.\n\nSimultaneously, the laser penetrates the skin's deeper dermis layer, heating it to stimulate the growth of new collagen fibers. Collagen is essential for firming and smoothing skin. As the epidermis heals and regrows, the treated skin appears clearer, smoother, and tighter. Fractional CO2 lasers, a newer version, pixelate the beam into thousands of tiny shafts of light that penetrate deeper, pushing out old damaged skin and replacing it with new, while also shrinking existing collagen. This promotes the body's natural healing process and collagen production.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0040-62-12136:1": 4.181485116738875, "clueweb22-en0004-59-04797:1": 3.9357161921737904, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:0": 3.913818266416949, "clueweb22-en0020-47-00301:9": 3.8887585580799815, "clueweb22-en0031-65-04139:2": 3.865045841127461, "clueweb22-en0040-62-12136:2": 3.8421660015456696, "clueweb22-en0018-50-01341:4": 3.8195747553068387}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0025-02-00163:1": 4.460971983793509, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:2": 4.300854714301749, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:13": 4.272477485338417, "clueweb22-en0040-62-12136:1": 4.181485116738875, "clueweb22-en0032-14-04213:7": 4.121401951442197, "clueweb22-en0037-37-03816:4": 4.085255823308207, "clueweb22-en0032-14-04213:8": 4.080063433064563, "clueweb22-en0002-32-13360:18": 4.077280813195451, "clueweb22-en0004-59-04797:1": 3.9357161921737904, "clueweb22-en0