{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You should avoid using your salicylic acid face wash immediately after microneedling. Products containing salicylic acid, other exfoliating acids (like AHAs), or strong acne treatments can irritate your skin and hinder the healing process, as your skin will be extra sensitive. It's generally recommended to wait at least 2-3 days, or even up to a week, before reintroducing such products. During this time, use a mild, gentle cleanser.\n\nFor your oily skin, after microneedling, your skin is more vulnerable, so it's best to avoid products that could be pore-clogging or irritating, such as those with petroleum-based, mineral oil, propylene glycol, or silicon-based ingredients. Also, avoid alcohol-containing skincare products, as they can cause burning and dryness. Focus on gentle, hydrating products like hyaluronic acid, peptides, and ceramides.\n\nRegarding your oily scalp and hair, you should refrain from your regular hair care routines immediately after microneedling, especially if the treatment area extends to your hairline or scalp. This includes avoiding direct high heat from tools like blow dryers, as well as very hot showers or steam rooms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:11": 4.730775222805704, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:12": 4.598413303365556, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:7": 4.503507318442376, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:10": 4.325050328144167, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:5": 4.162817062653348, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:2": 4.144491614346431, "clueweb22-en0023-06-19151:1": 4.099404802241637, "clueweb22-en0001-02-00582:10": 3.793121853423834, "clueweb22-en0019-72-05705:9": 3.77241706824076, "clueweb22-en0030-73-16433:6": 3.7291334712827595, "clueweb22-en0033-70-02855:4": 3.5492946544890964, "clueweb22-en0016-51-13074:5": 3.4880899961886906, "clueweb22-en0009-89-01915:8": 3.4097113325494695, "clueweb22-en00