{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The Pomodoro Technique is a time management system designed to help you focus on one task at a time and avoid feeling overwhelmed. Here's how it generally works:\n\n1.  **Choose a Task:** Pick one specific task you want to work on. The goal is to focus solely on this task without switching.\n2.  **Set a Timer:** Set a timer for 25 minutes. This 25-minute period is called a \"Pomodoro.\"\n3.  **Work with Focus:** For the next 25 minutes, concentrate only on your chosen task. If a distraction comes to mind, quickly write it down and return your attention to the task.\n4.  **Take a Short Break:** When the 25-minute timer rings, take a short 5-minute break.\n5.  **Repeat and Longer Break:** After completing four \"Pomodoro\" sessions (four 25-minute work periods with short breaks in between), take a longer break of 20-30 minutes.\n\nThe technique helps by breaking down work into manageable, focused intervals, encouraging single-tasking, and providing regular breaks to prevent burnout and maintain concentration.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 2.7378166865936198, "clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:19": 2.6470257284676864, "clueweb22-en0026-06-01592:6": 2.552729308531018, "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4": 2.5465248148281128, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 2.5170391603419895, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:20": 2.4534121543067404}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 5.0, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:5": 3.4451876788495803, "clueweb22-en0001-23-08745:1": 3.190737257639839, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:19": 3.1200509830031176, "clueweb22-en0015-94-05578:2": 2.8384546861902105, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 2.7378166865936198, "clueweb22-en0008-12-01882:6": 2.7176850645834723, "clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:12": 2.7122180995706815, "clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:19": 2.6470257284676864, "clueweb22-en000