{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You're right, the Pomodoro Technique, while helpful for some, can indeed be counterproductive if it interrupts a valuable state of hyperfocus. Many people with ADHD find that enforced breaks can make it difficult to get back into a task once they've finally achieved focus.\n\nInstead of relying on a strict timer, one effective approach is to break down your tasks into very small, manageable goals and give yourself a deadline for each, but without rigid scheduling. This allows you to work through tasks at your own pace, especially when you're in a state of deep concentration, without the pressure of an alarm forcing you to stop. The key is to find a system that works for *your* unique ADHD brain, rather than trying to force a method that doesn't align with your natural work patterns.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0015-94-05578:2": 4.208069435217092}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0015-94-05578:2": 4.208069435217092, "clueweb22-en0008-67-15474:5": 3.8542036085929667, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 3.845151825182544, "clueweb22-en0011-94-16617:3": 3.562247763488447, "clueweb22-en0012-91-02398:18": 3.4298198731295653, "clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:8": 3.429027124475101, "clueweb22-en0011-92-19024:14": 3.394329893728563, "clueweb22-en0005-65-02023:11": 3.3803266994830716, "clueweb22-en0027-34-14560:2": 3.3340479616717724, "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:3": 3.318305219990938, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:19": 3.308835867930291, "clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:12": 3.3017467024629905, "clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:11": 3.218573376419176, "clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:12": 3.184904240929699, "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4": 3.167505252595081, "clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:7": 3.136443378689156, "clueweb22-en0029-26-11797:14": 3.009692214579794, "clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:5": 2.980147184734969, "clueweb22-en0027-34-14560:1": 2.9672