{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-2_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To get started with tattooing, the foundational step is to cultivate your artistic skills. You must be a skilled artist, practicing drawing, painting, sketching, and digital art to develop a strong artistic eye and unique style.\n\nNext, build a comprehensive portfolio showcasing your artwork, specifically designs that would work well as tattoos. This portfolio is crucial for securing an apprenticeship or gaining admission to a tattoo school.\n\nThe most common and valuable path is to secure an apprenticeship with a certified tattoo artist. During an apprenticeship, you'll learn drawing techniques, professional business skills, best hygienic work practices, and how to use and sterilize equipment. Expect tough competition and that apprenticeships can last a few years.\n\nAlternatively, or in addition to an apprenticeship, you can take tattoo training courses offered by major cities or online. These courses cover the history, theories, fundamentals, and safety practices of tattooing.\n\nBefore working on human skin, practice extensively on fake skin, pigskin, or even fruits like apples and pears to develop basic tattooing skills such as outlining, coloring, and shading.\n\nFinally, once you complete your apprenticeship or course, you'll need to get certified and registered with your local council to obtain the necessary license to work as a professional tattoo artist.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-22-17473:2": 4.778322962454208, "clueweb22-en0028-52-08765:3": 4.695486202407197, "clueweb22-en0028-52-08765:4": 4.634986524106521, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:1": 4.496896683714321, "clueweb22-en0042-99-10026:9": 4.473240039500522, "clueweb22-en0024-21-00136:7": 4.447223266270812, "clueweb22-en0028-52-08765:6": 4.397348589304734, "clueweb22-en0025-87-09139:2": 4.387721450988702, "clueweb22-en0019-79-04825:1": 4.32509509673848