{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For comfortable mountain biking on forest trails and rough paths, you'll want a saddle specifically designed for mountain bikes. These saddles typically feature sufficient padding, especially for your sit bones, to absorb the bumps and vibrations from uneven terrain (Passages 1, 2, 4, 6, 10, 16).\n\nMountain bike saddles are generally more padded than road bike saddles and are built with durability in mind, often having long-lasting, weatherproof covers to withstand challenging conditions (Passages 1, 4, 7, 10, 16). They may also have smoother edges to prevent snagging and scuff guards for added protection (Passage 12).\n\nWhen choosing, look for features like pressure-relieving channels and consider saddles with \"active technology\" that allows for some flex with your pedaling motion (Passages 7, 8, 11). Knowing your sit-bone width is also crucial, as the right saddle width will provide optimal support (Passage 14).\n\nIt's generally recommended to avoid traditional leather saddles, like those from Brooks, for mountain biking, as they often lack the necessary padding for rough trails (Passage 18). Finding the perfect saddle can sometimes involve a bit of trial and error to match your anatomy and riding style (Passages 3, 8, 13).", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-67-05830:2": 4.0843392069807045, "clueweb22-en0007-52-02129:8": 4.0247405284573885, "clueweb22-en0044-55-03283:1": 3.8668474433108857, "clueweb22-en0007-05-17998:10": 3.771656364686731, "clueweb22-en0007-52-02129:7": 3.7572725380065997, "clueweb22-en0007-05-17998:4": 3.7335183230024236, "clueweb22-en0007-05-17998:1": 3.712470830117339, "clueweb22-en0040-31-08734:3": 3.6435351121095594, "clueweb22-en0020-10-04236:16": 3.6163966392173252, "clueweb22-en0044-50-07094:2": 3.6004361657109385, "clueweb22-en0044-55-03283:0": 3.5450589613086927, "clueweb22-en0009-83-153