{"metadata": {"team_id": "ucsc", "run_id": "UCSC-SIMRAG-ensemble", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To use your chain breaker tool and open your bike chain, follow these steps:\n\nFirst, understand that your chain consists of outer plates, inner plates, rollers, and pins. The chain tool works by pushing one of these pins out of the rollers to allow the chain to separate.\n\n1.  **Position the chain:** Your chain tool has two prongs next to a small metal pin. Fit one of your chain links between these prongs, ensuring it's securely in place and the prongs align with the gaps on either side of the link.\n2.  **Align the driving pin:** Line up the driving pin of the chain tool precisely with the center of one of the chain's rivets (pins). You might need to retract the driving pin by unscrewing part of the tool first. Ensure the driving pin is centered on the rivet head.\n3.  **Push the pin:** Turn the handle of the chain tool clockwise. This will push the pin out of the link. Continue turning until the rivet is forced out of the front plate and partially through the rear plate.\n4.  **Break the link:** Before completely removing the rivet, turn the handle counterclockwise to withdraw the driving pin. Then, grab the chain on either side of the link with your thumbs and wiggle it back and forth until the link separates. Be careful not to deform or twist the chain.\n\nThis method will allow you to open your chain to adjust its length.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 4.435159204881876, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:3": 4.279354986021573, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:3": 4.018575573671867, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:6": 3.8931396693228, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:6": 3.848318842487879}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 4.435159204881876, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:8": 4.412241509397069, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:3": 4.394955304353587, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:11": 4.34467556244